d":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Document ID → List of Terms","locale":"en"},"1328":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-85","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Inverted","locale":"en"},"1329":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-86","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Term → List of Document IDs","locale":"en"},"1330":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-87","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"This inversion is what makes keyword-based search efficient. Instead of checking every document to see if it contains your query term, you jump straight to the term and get all matching documents immediately.","locale":"en"},"1331":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-88","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"While powerful, inverted indexes come with costs:","locale":"en"},"1332":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-89","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Storage overhead**: The index requires additional storage space.","locale":"en"},"1333":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-90","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Write amplification**: Every write operation — `INSERT`, `UPSERT`, and `UPDATE` — require index maintenance, which adds latency to writes and increases I/O load.","locale":"en"},"1334":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"page","content":"Vector Embedding","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","locale":"en"},"1335":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","content":"A numerical representation of unstructured data that captures semantic meaning for similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1336":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"What is a Vector?","locale":"en"},"1337":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"How Do You Use Vectors with a Database?","locale":"en"},"1338":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"How Vectors Power Real-World Applications?","locale":"en"},"1339":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"What is an Embedding Model?","locale":"en"},"1340":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Types of Vectors","locale":"en"},"1341":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense Vectors","locale":"en"},"1342":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1343":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"In the context of AI and vector databases, &#x2A;**a vector is a list of numbers generated by embedding models to capture the semantic essence of unstructured data*** —  such as text, images, or audio.","locale":"en"},"1344":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"These models transform raw input into a high-dimensional space where &#x2A;**semantically similar items produce similar vectors***, enabling AI systems to compare meaning rather than relying on exact word matches.","locale":"en"},"1345":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🗂️ **Store**: Generate embeddings from your data — documents, product images, or user profiles — and save them in the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1346":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🔍 **Search**: When a new query arrives (a question, photo, etc.), generate a **query vector** using the same embedding model, then ask the database to find the most similar vectors.","locale":"en"},"1347":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"Using efficient indexes, the database quickly returns relevant results — even at large scale. This is the foundation of semantic search: **finding what &#x2A;**means**&#x2A; the same, not just what &#x2A;**says*** the same**.","locale":"en"},"1348":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"**Image search** is a great example:","locale":"en"},"1349":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Each image is converted into a vector that captures its visual features — such as shape, color, and object type.","locale":"en"},"1350":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Images that are **visually or semantically similar end up with nearby vectors**.","locale":"en"},"1351":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"By comparing these vectors, search systems can:","locale":"en"},"1352":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Recognize the same person across different photos**: Even with changes in lighting, pose, or expression, images of one individual generate similar vectors, allowing the system to match identities reliably.","locale":"en"},"1353":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Find look-alike products in e-commerce platforms**: When a user snaps a photo of a dress, lamp, or sofa, the system compares its vector to product vectors and retrieves items with similar appearance or style.","locale":"en"},"1354":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"All of this happens through fast vector similarity comparisons, powered by the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1355":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"An embedding model is an AI model that converts raw data into vector embeddings — illustrated in the diagram at the top.","locale":"en"},"1356":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"These models learn patterns from vast amounts of training data so that objects with similar meanings produce vectors that are close together in vector space — typically measured using distance metrics such as **cosine similarity**, **dot product**, or **Euclidean distance**.","locale":"en"},"1357":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"**The choice of distance metric matters.** If an embedding model was trained for a specific metric (e.g., cosine similarity), the vector database should use the same metric during search to preserve semantic relationships and achieve optimal accuracy.","locale":"en"},"1358":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"To explore and compare state-of-the-art embedding models, you can check out the Embedding Leaderboard on Hugging Face, which evaluates hundreds of models across diverse tasks and languages.","locale":"en"},"1359":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Vector representations are primarily categorized into two types: &#x2A;**dense**&#x2A; and &#x2A;**sparse***, each capturing data in its own way.","locale":"en"},"1360":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense vectors are fixed-length, real-valued embeddings where (nearly) every dimension carries semantic information. These vectors are often generated by deep learning models that transform raw inputs (e.g., text, images, audio) into a structured vector space reflecting their semantic similarities.","locale":"en"},"1361":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**✅ Semantic-Rich**: understands context and meaning (e.g., \"king – man + woman ≈ queen\")","locale":"en"},"1362":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Opaque**: hard to interpret which features drive similarity","locale":"en"},"1363":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse vectors are high-dimensional, often vocabulary-sized representations in which only a small subset of dimensions are non-zero. Each active dimension corresponds to a specific term (e.g., a word or n-gram), weighted by relevance scores such as **BM25**.","locale":"en"},"1364":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"In this model, every document is converted into a vector — called a document vector — that records which terms appear in it and how important they are. Similarly, a search query is also turned into a sparse vector using the same weighting scheme.","locale":"en"},"1365":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Rather than relying on exact keyword matches, similarity between a query and a document is computed using the dot product of their vectors. This measures how well their weighted terms align: documents that contain the same important terms as the query receive higher scores — rewarding both **term overlap** and **term importance**.","locale":"en"},"1366":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"For computational efficiency, sparse vectors use integer indices to map terms to their positions within a vocabulary dictionary rather than storing the term strings directly.","locale":"en"},"1367":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**✅ Interpretable**: non-zero dimensions map directly to known terms (e.g., `4017` → \"puppy\")","locale":"en"},"1368":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Lacks Semantic Understanding**: treats \"car\" and \"automobile\" as unrelated unless explicitly linked","locale":"en"},"1369":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","type":"page","content":"Destroy","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","locale":"en"},"1370":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","content":"Destroying a collection **permanently deletes it from disk**. This operation **cannot be undone**.","locale":"en"},"1371":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","content":"**Warning**: All data in the collection will be lost. Ensure you no longer need the collection or have created a backup before calling `destroy()`.","locale":"en"},"1372":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","content":"After calling `destroy()`, the collection directory and its contents are removed from the filesystem.","locale":"en"},"1373":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/destroy","content":"Do not use the `collection` object afterward — it is no longer valid.","locale":"en"},"1374":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","type":"page","content":"Collections","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections","locale":"en"},"1375":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"A **collection** is a named container for documents in Zvec.","locale":"en"},"1376":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"Think of a collection as a table in a relational database: it's where you **store, organize, and query your data**.","locale":"en"},"1377":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"This section covers the operations for managing collections.","locale":"en"},"1378":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Create a New Collection\" href=\"./create/\" icon=\"<FolderPlus className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1379":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Open an Existing Collection\" href=\"./open/\" icon=\"<FolderOpen className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1380":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Inspect a Collection\" href=\"./inspect/\" icon=\"<Eye className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1381":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Destroy a Collection\" href=\"./destroy/\" icon=\"<Trash className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1382":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Optimize a Collection\" href=\"./optimize/\" icon=\"<Zap className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1383":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections","content":"<Card title=\"Schema Evolution\" href=\"./schema-evolution/\" icon=\"<Wrench className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"1384":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"page","content":"Inspect","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","locale":"en"},"1385":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Quick Reference","locale":"en"},"1386":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-schema","content":"Collection Schema","locale":"en"},"1387":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-statistics","content":"Collection Statistics","locale":"en"},"1388":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-options","content":"Collection Options","locale":"en"},"1389":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-path","content":"Collection Path","locale":"en"},"1390":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","content":"Once you've opened a collection, you can inspect its structure, configuration, and runtime state to better understand how it's organized and performing. This is especially helpful during development, debugging, or system monitoring.","locale":"en"},"1391":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Property","locale":"en"},"1392":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"1393":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"`Collection.schema`","locale":"en"},"1394":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Collection structure and field definitions (e.g., vector dimensions, data types)","locale":"en"},"1395":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"`Collection.stats`","locale":"en"},"1396":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Runtime metrics such as document count and index completeness","locale":"en"},"1397":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"`Collection.option`","locale":"en"},"1398":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Runtime settings (e.g., read-only mode, memory mapping)","locale":"en"},"1399":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"`Collection.path`","locale":"en"},"1400":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#quick-reference","content":"Filesystem path to the collection directory","locale":"en"},"1401":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-schema","content":"To view the schema:","locale":"en"},"1402":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-schema","content":"`\"name\": \"my_collection\"`: The name of the collection.","locale":"en"},"1403":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-schema","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1404":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-schema","content":"`\"price\"`: A **required** 32-bit integer, with inverted index and range query optimization enabled.","locale":"en"},"1405":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect",