"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"Zvec supports **dynamic schema evolution**, allowing you to modify a collection's structure after it has been created — without downtime, data re-ingestion, or reindexing.","locale":"en"},"1471":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"You can:","locale":"en"},"1472":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Add or drop scalar fields**","locale":"en"},"1473":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Rename fields** or **change their data types** ((as long as the change is safe — e.g., from `INT32` to `INT64`)","locale":"en"},"1474":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Create or drop indexes on fields**","locale":"en"},"1475":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"❌  Add or drop vector fields (🔜 coming soon)","locale":"en"},"1476":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"In Zvec, schema changes are performed using &#x2A;*Data Definition Language (DDL)** methods, grouped into two categories:","locale":"en"},"1477":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Column DDL**: defines *what data you store*.\\\nIt manages the structure of your collection by adding, removing, renaming or altering fields.","locale":"en"},"1478":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Index DDL**: defines *how you search that data*.\\\nIt controls the creation and removal of indexes on fields.","locale":"en"},"1479":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"💡 **Indexing Rules in Zvec**","locale":"en"},"1480":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Every vector field must be indexed** using an appropriate vector index to enable similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1481":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Scalar fields are optionally indexed** — but you should build inverted indexes on any scalar field you plan to use in filtering queries (e.g., `WHERE category = 'music'`).","locale":"en"},"1482":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes you have opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1483":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#prerequisites","content":"This example collection includes a scalar field `publish_year`.","locale":"en"},"1484":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"To add a new scalar field to an existing collection, use `add_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1485":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"`field_schema`:\\\nDefines the name and data type of the new field. See scalar field schema for details.","locale":"en"},"1486":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"`expression`:\\\nSpecifies the default value for existing documents. Since they don't already have a `rating` field, Zvec uses this `expression` to fill in the missing values — in this case, setting `rating = 5` for all current documents.","locale":"en"},"1487":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"Currently, only **numerical scalar fields** can be added via `add_column()`. Support for `string` and `boolean` types is coming soon.\\\nAccordingly, the `expression` must evaluate to a number — it can be a single numerical literal (like `\"5\"`) or a simple arithmetic expression involving existing numerical fields (e.g., `\"publish_year + 1\"`).","locale":"en"},"1488":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-a-column","content":"To permanently remove a scalar field, use `drop_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1489":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-a-column","content":"This **deletes the field and all its data from every document** in the collection. The operation is **irreversible**.","locale":"en"},"1490":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#alter-a-column","content":"To rename a column or update its schema, use `alter_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1491":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#view-the-current-schema","content":"After making changes, you can always check your collection's current structure by printing its schema:","locale":"en"},"1492":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#view-the-current-schema","content":"See schema example for more details.","locale":"en"},"1493":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"To accelerate search performance, you can create (or replace) indexes on both **vector** and **scalar** fields using `create_index()`:","locale":"en"},"1494":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"**Vector fields** must use one of the following index types:","locale":"en"},"1495":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`HnswIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1496":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`HnswRabitqIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1497":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`IVFIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1498":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`FlatIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1499":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"**Scalar fields** use `InvertIndexParam` to enable efficient filtering.","locale":"en"},"1500":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-an-index","content":"To remove an index from a scalar field, use `drop_index()`:","locale":"en"},"1501":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-an-index","content":"**It is not allowed to drop the index of a vector field**.\\\nIn Zvec, every vector field must always have exactly one index to support similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1502":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"page","content":"Delete","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","locale":"en"},"1503":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Delete by IDs","locale":"en"},"1504":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Delete by Filter Condition","locale":"en"},"1505":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Zvec provides two ways to delete documents. Choose the method that best fits your use case:","locale":"en"},"1506":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"1507":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Input","locale":"en"},"1508":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"When to Use","locale":"en"},"1509":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete()`","locale":"en"},"1510":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"One or more document `id`s","locale":"en"},"1511":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use when you know the exact ID(s) of the documents you want to delete","locale":"en"},"1512":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete_by_filter()`","locale":"en"},"1513":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"A filter expression (e.g., `publish_year < 1900`)","locale":"en"},"1514":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use for bulk deletion based on field values — ideal for cleaning up documents that match specific criteria","locale":"en"},"1515":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Delete operations are **immediate** and **irreversible**.\\\nAlways double-check your input before running a delete operation.","locale":"en"},"1516":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Assume you've already opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1517":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Use `delete()` to remove one or more documents when you know their exact IDs.","locale":"en"},"1518":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a single `id`, `delete()` returns one `Status` object.","locale":"en"},"1519":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a list of `id`s, it returns a list of `Status` objects in the same order.","locale":"en"},"1520":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Use `delete_by_filter()` to remove all documents that match a boolean `filter` expression.","locale":"en"},"1521":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"The `filter` can reference scalar fields (e.g., `publish_year`, `language`) using comparison and logical operators.","locale":"en"},"1522":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","type":"page","content":"Fetch","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","locale":"en"},"1523":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Use `fetch()` to retrieve documents by their `id`s.\\\nThis is a **direct lookup** — no search, scoring, or filtering is involved.","locale":"en"},"1524":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Input**: A single document `id` or a list of document `id`s.","locale":"en"},"1525":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Output**: A mapping from each **found** `id` to its corresponding document object.","locale":"en"},"1526":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Missing `id`s are **silently omitted** from the result (no error raised).","locale":"en"},"1527":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"The returned dictionary does not guarantee input order — access documents by `id` instead.","locale":"en"},"1528":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","type":"page","content":"Data Operations","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","locale":"en"},"1529":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Zvec provides a complete set of **data manipulation operations** to manage documents in your collection.","locale":"en"},"1530":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"1531":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"1532":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Insert`","locale":"en"},"1533":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Add new documents (fails if the document `ID` already exists)","locale":"en"},"1534":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Upsert`","locale":"en"},"1535":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Insert new documents or replace existing ones by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1536":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Update`","locale":"en"},"1537":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Modify specific fields of existing documents by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1538":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Delete`","locale":"en"},"1539":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Delete documents by `ID` or using a scalar filter condition","locale":"en"},"1540":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Query`","locale":"en"},"1541":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Perform vector similarity search or full-text search, optionally combined with scalar filtering and re-ranking","locale":"en"},"1542":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Fetch`","locale":"en"},"1543":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Retrieve full documents directly by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1544":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Iterate`","locale":"en"},"1545":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Stream every document one by one without loading the whole collection into memory","locale":"en"},"1546":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"All write operations (`insert`, `upsert`, `update`, `delete`) are immediately visible for querying — enabling true real-time, streaming workloads.","locale":"en"},"1547":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"page","content":"Insert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","locale":"en"},"1548":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1549":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Insert a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1550":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Insert a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1551":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1552":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Multiple Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1553":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"Use the &#x2A;*`insert()`** method to add one or more new documents (`Doc`) to a collection.","locale":"en"},"1554":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"**Performance Tip**:\\\nNew vectors are initially buffered for fast ingestion. For optimal search performance, call `optimize()` after inserting a large batch of documents.","locale":"en"},"1555":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `insert()` must:","locale":"en"},"1556":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Have a unique `id` (not already present in the collection)","locale":"en"},"1557":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Provide data that matches the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1558":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1559":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1560":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"You can omit `nullable` scalar fields if a document doesn't have a value for them","locale":"en"},"1561":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"If a document with the same `id` already exists in the collection, the insertion will **fail** for that document.\\\nTo overwrite existing documents or insert without checking, use `upsert()` instead.","locale":"en"},"1562":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1563":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A scalar field: `text` (string)","locale":"en"},"1564":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A dense vector embedding: `text_embedding` (4-dimensional FP32 vector)","locale":"en"},"1565":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The 4-dimensional vector is for demonstration only — real-world embeddings are usually much larger.","locale":"en"},"1566":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"You've also opened the collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1567":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Now, insert a document like this:","locale":"en"},"1568":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The `insert()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1569":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1570":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the insertion and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., duplicate `ID`, insufficient disk space).","locale":"en"},"1571":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Successfully inserted documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1572":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To insert multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `insert()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1573":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are inserted**.","locale":"en"},"1574":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to insert every one. A failure in one (e.g., duplicate `id`) does **not** stop others from being inserted.","locale":"en"},"1575":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1576":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Assume your collection includes a sparse vector named `sparse_embedding`.","locale":"en"},"1577":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert a document with a sparse vector like this:","locale":"en"},"1578":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"A sparse vector is represented as a mapping from `dimension indices` (integers) to `values` (floats).\\\nThere is **no fixed dimension size** — only non-zero dimensions need to be included.","locale":"en"},"1579":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Real-world applications often require collections with multiple scalar fields and vector embeddings. In this example, assume your collection includes the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1580":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1581":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1582":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1583":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1584":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1585":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1586":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1587":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert a document with multiple fields and vectors like this:","locale":"en"},"1588":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"page","content":"Iterate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","locale":"en"},"1589":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"Select Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1590":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Snapshot Semantics","locale":"en"},"1591":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Concurrency","locale":"en"},"1592":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Break Early","locale":"en"},"1593":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Use &#x2A;*`iter_docs()`** to stream **all** documents in a collection one by one.","locale":"en"},"1594":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Unlike `fetch()` — which retrieves documents by known `id`s — iteration performs a **full scan**. Documents are streamed in bounded windows, so the whole collection is never materialized in memory at once — making it suitable for export, backup, migration, or offline processing.","locale":"en"},"1595":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"The iterator holds a native resource slot on the collection, so let the language close it for you: Python's `with` statement and JavaScript's `for...of` loop both release the iterator when the loop finishes, breaks early, or raises an exception. Iterators also close themselves automatically when fully exhausted.","locale":"en"},"1596":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"By default, every scalar field and every vector is materialized for each document. Use `output_fields` and `include_vector` to reduce the amount of data read:","locale":"en"},"1597":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`output_fields`** (`outputFields`): a list of scalar field names to return. If omitted, all scalar fields are returned; an empty list returns no scalar fields. Unknown or duplicate names raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1598":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`include_vector`** (`includeVector`): whether to materialize vector data. Vectors are included by default; disable it when you only need scalar fields — skipping vectors makes traversal faster.","locale":"en"},"1599":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Both `iter_docs()` and `iterDocsSync()` iterate over an **isolated snapshot taken at call time**:","locale":"en"},"1600":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Data written **after** the iterator is created — inserts, upserts, updates — is **not visible** to this iterator.","locale":"en"},"1601":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Deletes made after creation do not affect the iteration; documents already deleted when the snapshot was taken are filtered out.","locale":"en"},"1602":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"On a writable collection, creating the iterator may seal the current writing segment (each call can produce a new small segment); read-only collections are scanned directly without any write.","locale":"en"},"1603":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Iteration order is unspecified — it is **not** insertion order, and it can change after `optimize()` reorganizes segments — so never rely on it.","locale":"en"},"1604":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"While any iterator is open on a collection, these operations **raise an error**:","locale":"en"},"1605":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Schema changes — creating or dropping an index, adding, altering or dropping a column","locale":"en"},"1606":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"`optimize()`, which fails at its start","locale":"en"},"1607":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Closing or destroying the collection","locale":"en"},"1608":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Conversely, creating an iterator fails while one of those maintenance operations is already running. Writes, `flush()`, `query()` and `fetch()` remain **unaffected**.","locale":"en"},"1609":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Close every iterator before closing the collection. These restrictions are lifted as soon as all open iterators are closed.","locale":"en"},"1610":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Stopping before the end is safe — exiting the `with` block or the `for...of` loop releases the iterator's slot. When you drive the iterator manually instead, close it yourself:","locale":"en"},"1611":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"page","content":"Update","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","locale":"en"},"1612":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1613":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Update a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1614":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Update a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1615":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Use `update()` to modify **existing** documents (`Doc`).","locale":"en"},"1616":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Only the scalar fields and vector embeddings you **include will be updated**; all other content remains unchanged.","locale":"en"},"1617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"The method accepts either a single `Doc` object or a list of `Doc` objects.","locale":"en"},"1618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `update()` must:","locale":"en"},"1619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Specify an `id` that **already exists** in the collection (the operation will fail if the document is not found)","locale":"en"},"1620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Include only the fields and vectors you **intend to update**, formatted according to the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/dat