f=\"./group/\" icon=\"<Rows3 className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"page","content":"Multiple Vectors","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","locale":"en"},"2618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Performing Multi-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranking Strategies","locale":"en"},"2621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"Zvec supports **multi-vector queries**, allowing you to combine different embeddings in a single search.","locale":"en"},"2622":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"When querying multiple vector embeddings, Zvec retrieves candidates from each vector space independently and then fuses them into one relevance-ordered list. Because scores from different vector spaces might not be directly comparable, you must choose a suitable **re-ranking strategy**.","locale":"en"},"2623":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes:","locale":"en"},"2624":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You have opened a `collection` with multiple vector fields","locale":"en"},"2625":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You're familiar with the basic vector querying concepts. If not, please review the single-vector search guide","locale":"en"},"2626":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2627":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2628":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2629":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2630":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"In Python, pass a list of query specifications to `query()` and provide a fusion strategy through `reranker`. In Node.js, pass the sub-queries to `multiQuerySync()` or `multiQuery()` and configure `rerank`.","locale":"en"},"2631":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"This example queries both `dense_embedding` and `sparse_embedding` and uses `WeightedReRanker` to combine their results. Weights are positional and must follow the same order as `queries`.","locale":"en"},"2632":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topk` always controls the number of **final documents** returned after fusion.","locale":"en"},"2633":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Python does not currently expose a separate candidate-count option for each sub-query in `Collection.query()`.","locale":"en"},"2634":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Node.js supports `numCandidates` on each sub-query. If omitted, its default is `max(topk, 10)`.","locale":"en"},"2635":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topn` is used only when calling a re-ranker's standalone `rerank()` method; it is not a constructor argument.","locale":"en"},"2636":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Zvec provides different re-ranking strategies to combine scores from multiple vector fields.","locale":"en"},"2637":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranker","locale":"en"},"2638":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`WeightedReRanker`","locale":"en"},"2639":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`RrfReRanker` (Reciprocal Rank Fusion)","locale":"en"},"2640":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Approach","locale":"en"},"2641":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Combines normalized similarity scores using **custom weights**","locale":"en"},"2642":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Fuses results based only on **ranking positions** — no scores needed  With a zero-based rank *r* (the first result is 0), the RRF score is: $\\text{RRF}(r) = \\frac{1}{k + r + 1}$","locale":"en"},"2643":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"2644":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores are reasonably comparable across vector fields  • You know the relative importance of each embedding type","locale":"en"},"2645":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores come from different metrics or scales  • You prefer a simple, robust, tuning-free method","locale":"en"},"2646":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2647":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`weights`: An ordered list aligned with `queries`. Score normalization uses each queried field's schema.","locale":"en"},"2648":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`rank_constant` (*k*): Controls how quickly rank influence decreases. Higher values reduce the dominance of top-ranked results.","locale":"en"},"2649":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"page","content":"Single Vector","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","locale":"en"},"2650":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2651":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Performing Single-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2652":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2653":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-o